Sumālin roams mortals with nubile Kaikasī --- Sumālin sees glorious Vaiśravaṇa on Puṣpaka --- Sumālin bids daughter choose Viśravas herself --- Kaikasī approaches fire-tending Viśravas bowed --- Viśravas foretells cruel sons from dread hour --- Kaikasī wins righteous last son boon --- Father names ten-headed infant Daśagrīva amid dire omens --- Huge Kumbhakarṇa devours seers, hideous Śūrpaṇakhā follows, righteous Vibhīṣaṇa studies --- Kaikasī spurs Rāvaṇa to match Vaiśravaṇa --- Rāvaṇa vows supremacy and seeks Gōkarṇa penance